cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use esMorph in research or software, please cite it."
title: "esMorph, a fast morphological analyzer for Spanish"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shkarin
    given-names: Sergey
    email: kouki.sergey@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/SergeyShk/esMorph"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - spanish
  - nlp
  - morphology
  - morphological analysis
  - lemmatization
  - inflection
  - conjugation
  - universal dependencies
  - wiktionary
  - rust
abstract: "esMorph is a morphological analyzer of Spanish with a Rust core and a Python API: for a word form it finds the analyses in a dictionary - the lemma, the part of speech and the Universal Dependencies features - and gives the forms of a lexeme by their features. Work in progress."
